                "statement": "Other accounts with several incoming senders did not reach the threshold and have no fan-in indicator: A-9862 (4 senders: T0021, T0024, T0025, T0026) and A-1823 (3 senders, 6 transfers). A-4989, where A-9278's routes end, also has no indicator.",
                "claim_ids": [
                  "AB6",
                  "AB7",
                  "AB8"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "hypotheses": [
              {
                "id": "H1",
                "statement": "The A-9278 pattern fits a pass-through or layering route under shared control: money from several senders is collected and forwarded in a few minutes, across three hops, from one device, ending at A-4989. The data does not establish control, ownership or fraud. A shared device is only a recorded relationship.",
                "references": [
                  "F4",
                  "F6",
                  "F8",
                  "S1"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "H2",
                "statement": "The A-9895 pattern (six identical 2500 payments from different senders, with one 14000 payment out) may be ordinary collection, such as a group payment or a split bill. It is weaker evidence of layering than A-9278. This is an interpretation, not a finding.",
                "references": [
                  "F3",
                  "F5",
                  "F7"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "H3",
                "statement": "The small drop at each A-9278 hop (about 3000–4000 per hop) could be fees or skimming. The data does not record why.",
                "references": [
                  "F4"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "unresolved": [
              {
                "id": "U1",
                "question": "Where did T0041's funding come from? It pays 14000, but its three linked credits (T0038–T0040) total only 7500. Onward links are matched on time only and do not show which money was actually forwarded.",
                "references": [
                  "P3",
                  "E41"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "U2",
                "question": "What happens to the money at A-4989 and A-1415 outside this bounded replay? A-4989 sends nothing in the dataset. A-1415's later T0055 (90000 to A-9514) is too late to be linked, and its source is not recorded.",
                "references": [
                  "AB2",
                  "AB4",
                  "E55"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "U3",
                "question": "Who controls device D-568, and do A-9278, A-5092 and A-2897 share one owner? The data records device use only, not identity.",
                "references": [
                  "S1"
                ]
              }
